Lota's LZ4 patch: two statements of src/libraries/lz4/lz4.c, the LZ4 1.8.0
that LÖVE bundles (lz4.h, lines 94-96), each backported from LZ4 itself.
LZ4_compress_generic computes the end of its dictionary as dictionary +
dictSize (line 549), and LZ4_decompress_generic as dictStart + dictSize
(line 1192), even when there is no dictionary and the pointer is null.
Every one-shot compress adds 0 to a null pointer at line 549,
LZ4_decompress_safe adds 0 at line 1192, and LZ4_decompress_fast, which
passes a null dictStart with a dictSize of 64 KB (line 1362), adds 65536
there. C leaves all three undefined, and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops
rake test:native at them: Apple clang 17 and LLVM clang 18 report adding
0, and every clang reports adding 65536
(doc/contributors/upstream/016.md). Nothing outside lz4.c can reach those
statements: LÖVE's love::data::Compressor calls LZ4_compress_default,
LZ4_compress_HC, LZ4_decompress_safe, and LZ4_decompress_fast
(src/modules/data/Compressor.cpp, lines 74-78 and 132-153), which
Lota::Data.compress and Lota::Data.decompress reach, and the arithmetic is
inside them.

The first hunk is the first statement of LZ4's own commit
e68c7d38780ada518e6c43a09a2d92421ea8111b ("avoid computing 0 offsets from
null pointers", Alexander Gallego, 2020, first in LZ4 1.9.3; lib/lz4.c
line 822 there, line 880 in 1.9.3), where LZ4 had by then made
cctx->dictSize a local dictSize. The second is one statement of LZ4's
own commit 8bea19d57c0db6d3d812c7acc3d1834762bce297 ("fixed minor
cppcheck warnings in lib", Yann Collet, 2018, first in LZ4 1.9.0;
lib/lz4.c line 1426 there, line 1761 in 1.9.3), which covers
LZ4_decompress_fast's 64 KB as well as LZ4_decompress_safe's 0, since it
tests the pointer and not the size. Each leaves the end of a dictionary
that is not there null, as the arithmetic made it, so neither changes a
byte LZ4 writes or reads, and nothing else in those commits is needed to
remove the three reports. Like LZ4 itself, the patch is under the
BSD-2-Clause license (lz4.c, lines 1-33). CMake applies it to a copy of
the file at configure time (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love
is never written to. Drop it when LÖVE updates its bundled LZ4 to 1.9.3
or later, which has both statements.

diff -ruN a/src/libraries/lz4/lz4.c b/src/libraries/lz4/lz4.c
--- a/src/libraries/lz4/lz4.c
+++ b/src/libraries/lz4/lz4.c
@@ -546,7 +546,7 @@
     const BYTE* lowLimit;
     const BYTE* const lowRefLimit = ip - cctx->dictSize;
     const BYTE* const dictionary = cctx->dictionary;
-    const BYTE* const dictEnd = dictionary + cctx->dictSize;
+    const BYTE* const dictEnd = dictionary ? dictionary + cctx->dictSize : dictionary;
     const ptrdiff_t dictDelta = dictEnd - (const BYTE*)source;
     const BYTE* anchor = (const BYTE*) source;
     const BYTE* const iend = ip + inputSize;
@@ -1189,7 +1189,7 @@
     BYTE* cpy;
     BYTE* oexit = op + targetOutputSize;
 
-    const BYTE* const dictEnd = (const BYTE*)dictStart + dictSize;
+    const BYTE* const dictEnd = (dictStart == NULL) ? NULL : dictStart + dictSize;
     const unsigned inc32table[8] = {0, 1, 2,  1,  0,  4, 4, 4};
     const int      dec64table[8] = {0, 0, 0, -1, -4,  1, 2, 3};
 
